Feature: Takeoff and return
  +TKOF puts a takeoff at home at the start of the plan. Its altitude is the plan altitude,
  but not more than 40 m. With a [[hand launch]], the takeoff waits for the throw. +RTL adds
  a return to launch at the end of the plan. Then the plane comes back to the point where
  you armed it.

  Expectation: +TKOF puts a takeoff first
    Given the takeoff is not planned
    When the operator adds a takeoff
    Then the plan goes up by 1
    And the takeoff is planned

  Expectation: The plan has only one takeoff
    Given the takeoff is planned
    When the operator adds a takeoff
    Then the plan stays the same

  Expectation: On an empty plan the takeoff is also the last item
    Given the takeoff is not planned
    And the plan has 0 items
    When the operator adds a takeoff
    Then the plan has 1 item
    And the last plan item is TAKEOFF

  Expectation: +RTL ends the plan with a return
    When the operator adds a return home
    Then the plan goes up by 1
    And the last plan item is RTL
